-- **Extra layers → NavAid pilots → Show public NavAid pilots** draws every public aircraft, with
+- **Extra layers → NavAid pilots → Share & see** does both halves in one tap: it makes you public
+  (starting a share if none is running) and draws every public aircraft, with
   its identifier and speed · altitude beside it (the icon points along its true track). They grow a
   little as you zoom in. A silent aircraft fades after 2 minutes and says how long ago it was last
   heard (`95 kt · 2500 ft · 4 min`); after 30 minutes it goes.
-- **Seeing others needs sharing publicly yourself.** Until you do, the switch is dimmed and says
-  so. The one exception is the **secret viewing link**, `https://navaid.supino.org/?pilots=<secret>`:
+- **Seeing others needs sharing publicly yourself.** Until you do, **See others** is dimmed and says
+  so; **Off** takes you off the public channel and stops showing the others. The one exception is the **secret viewing link**, `https://navaid.supino.org/?pilots=<secret>`:
   it shows everyone without sharing, and fits the map to them. The app holds only the secret's
   SHA-256 (`publicPilotsViewHash`), so a new secret is a gist change.
 - **Your own aircraft is never drawn as someone else** — not even an old one: the phone remembers
